#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""t2: BackOtter's Test2 words, run on the Mac (contract 1.7; rulings R10, R21, R27).

  t2 WORD [ARG...] [plan] [--json] [--hosts H,H] [--universe CELL,...]
        GateTest2 [ROUND] [LAYER...] [stale] [plan]       GateTest2All [ROUND] [plan]
        SticTest2 [ROUND] [GUEST...] [stale] [plan]       SticTest2All [ROUND] [plan]
        HoltTest2 [GUEST[+VARIANT]...] [stale] [plan] [+bigger] [+oneshot] [+degraded] [+img] [--holt-bin DIR]
        HoltTest2X [X...] for X in D A M U Z F C V BSD H I G Obscure ARM  HoltTest2All [plan]
        GuestTest2 [GUEST...] [stale] [plan]              GuestTest2All [plan]
        GuestTest2 update [GUEST...] [plan]               the real update round
        ImgTest2 [PLAT...] [release] [stale] [plan]       ImgTest2All [release] [plan]
        BkoTest2 [ROUND] [stale] [plan]                   SweepTest2 [ROUND] [plan]
        (--universe is test-only: it cuts the word's cells down to those named)
        --harness-stop N (or T2_HARNESS_STOP=N): N harness-class results stop the run, in place
        of classes.json's policy.stop.harness_results, for every family and composite child; it
        enters no key, and run.log and the report say "harness stop: N (override; policy P)"
        --lock-wait T (90m, 2h, 45s; a bare number is seconds): a run another run's lock would
        refuse (exit 2, "holds its lock") waits up to T for that run to end, then starts with a
        fresh pull and facts: the family's lock, and for HoltTest2 words a cell another live run
        holds (without it that cell is planned not-runnable).  BkoTest2, SweepTest2 and
        `GuestTest2 update` wait before they start only.  Not in a batch entry (the batch waits)
  t2 plan WORD [ARG...]                  the same as WORD ... plan
  t2 pull                                each host's ledger mirrored, then the wear join
  t2 ledger show [--cell C] [--last N] [--json]
  t2 explain CELL [--hosts H,H] [--round R]
                                         its inputs against its last PASS, group by group
  t2 copy [--hosts H,H] [--gc]           the private copy of this checkout on the hosts
  t2 resume RUN [--harness-stop N] [--lock-wait T]
                                         a run picked up again (R10); t2b-/t2w-: the composite
                                         (no --lock-wait)
  t2 guest-lines RUN [--show [GUEST]] [--accept GUEST...|--accept-all]
                                         a GuestTest2 run's new log lines, and accepting them
  t2 guest-fingerprints [GUEST...] [--reproject]
                                         probe guests with no fingerprint at their generation
  t2 self-test                           tests/test_*.py (a process each, 6 at once), drive.py --self-test, the specs' checker,
                                         the fixtures' leak scan and the class table's check
  t2 ledger seed-current --family gate|stic|holt|guest|img [--perturb GROUP] [--cells C,...] [--age CELL=HOURS,...]
        [--round R] [--hosts H,H]        test only: synthetic PASS rows at the current keys
                                         (refused unless T2_MAC_ROOT is set and isn't the default)

--hosts H,H: of chopin, cinqcent, copland, cage, czerny, choubox, bigfoot (default
chopin,cinqcent,copland,cage,czerny,choubox: copland and cage since 2026-11-14,
choubox since 2026-11-17, czerny since 2026-11-19).  A new host
joins the defaults after HostTest2 and a representative per family pass there;
a small host (copland, cage, czerny, choubox: some cell's
reservation is over its cmp-run.sh ceiling) after the HostTest2 layers and one representative per
family pass among the cells that fit it, and the cells that don't fit it are placed on the other
hosts only, then too (choubox's own trial runs the user waived, its HostTest2 loop cells being
over its ceiling).  testvm/pick-host says which host has room for a run of your own right now.
Roots: T2_MAC_ROOT (~/backotter-work/test2), T2_HOST_ROOT (/bkoscratch/test2), T2_COPY_ROOT
(~/backotter-work/t2/copy), BKO_GIT (~/git).  Exit 0: PASS, nothing due or a plan printed;
1: a FAIL or FLAKY-FAIL, a to-class cell, or a stop rule stopped the run; 2: refused; 3: an internal error.
"""

